# Secure Web Infrastructure and WordPress Hardening Lab

This portfolio project documents the design, deployment, validation, and security review of a multi-VM Linux web environment built in Proxmox for a fictional client, Marconi Law Firm, LLC. The environment combines a Dockerized Ghost workload behind an Nginx reverse proxy with a separate Ubuntu LAMP server hosting WordPress. The technical steps, configurations, results, troubleshooting, and screenshots from the original report and demonstration video are integrated throughout this repository.

The project is presented as an operations-focused case study: successful controls are backed by evidence, the incomplete Ghost upstream path is clearly identified, and the remediation plan is documented instead of overstating the result.

## Executive summary

| Area | Delivered result |
| --- | --- |
| Virtualization | Three Linux virtual machines administered through Proxmox |
| Network | Private `10.10.229.0/24` lab with a dedicated gateway and static service addresses |
| Container platform | Docker Engine installed, enabled, and validated with `hello-world` |
| Reverse proxy | Nginx installed, running, and configured to proxy `/blog` to the Ghost application node |
| Web platform | Apache, MySQL, PHP, and WordPress deployed on Ubuntu |
| Hardening | WordPress permissions normalized, `wp-config.php` moved above the document root, and two security plugins activated |
| Troubleshooting | Ghost restart/exited state and resulting Nginx upstream error captured with a repeatable diagnostic runbook |

