## Security posture

This lab applied several useful controls, but it is a proof of concept rather than a production deployment. The polished documentation and configuration examples do not repeat the passwords contained in the source report. Before production use, the environment should also enforce SELinux, keep host firewalls enabled, terminate TLS, restrict management access, remove `.git` from the web root, pin tested software versions, centralize logs, and implement tested backups.

See the [Security assessment](docs/security-assessment.md) for a prioritized remediation table.

